# 📌 23. Key Takeaways

### AGI
AGI refers to AI capable of general-purpose intellectual abilities rather than being limited to a narrow task.

### Text Encoding
Converts characters into a representation computers can store and process.

### Tokenization
Breaks text into smaller units called tokens.

### Integer Encoding
Maps tokens to numerical IDs.

### Embeddings
Represent text as numerical vectors that capture semantic relationships.

### Foundation Models
Large pretrained models that can be adapted for many different applications.

### Fine-Tuning
Further trains a model to improve specialized behavior or task performance.

### RAG
Retrieves external information and supplies it to an AI model at query time.

### The Practical Rule

```text
Need better behavior?
        → Consider Fine-Tuning

Need external / changing knowledge?
        → Consider RAG

Need both?
        → Fine-Tuning + RAG
```

